# customer-template-billing

Full guidance: `.cursor/skills/rlm-customer-demo-billing/SKILL.md`.

## Status must be Draft

Salesforce rejects creating `BillingPolicy`, `BillingTreatment`, and
`BillingTreatmentItem` with `Status = Active`. The insert fails **silently** — SFDMU logs
"Totally processed 1 records" and nothing lands in the org.

Set `Status = Draft` in all three CSVs. `activate_customer_demo_billing` (step 6b) activates
in order BTI, BT, BP, setting `DefaultBillingTreatmentId` first.

## BillingTreatmentItem.CurrencyIsoCode is read-only

Omit it from the SFDMU SELECT and from the CSV header, or the BTI insert fails silently.

## Product2 billing assignment

`Product2.csv` is an Update setting `BillingPolicyId` via `BillingPolicy.Name`. Keep
`BillingPolicy` ahead of `Product2` in the same object set so SFDMU caches the new ID.

Failure signature: if the BillingPolicy insert failed, every Product2 Update row reports
**"Same data"** (null matching null) — a misleading success that hides the real error.

## Deletion

The delete script deactivates in reverse order (Policy to Draft plus clear
`DefaultBillingTreatmentId`, Treatment to Draft, TreatmentItem to Draft) before deleting.
Without deactivation, `Database.delete(..., false)` silently leaves Active records.

## Conventions

Name-based external IDs only — no Salesforce IDs in CSVs. Keep `skipExistingRecords: true`
on the core billing objects. `externalId` uses `;` delimiters.
